cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you refer to the LYNE Protocol, please cite the exact version you used, as below. The specification text is
  licensed under CC-BY-4.0; the schemas, test vectors, examples and conformance code under Apache-2.0 (LICENSE.md,
  REUSE.toml). Neither license grants rights to the LYNE name or visual identity (TRADEMARK_POLICY.md).
type: software
title: "LYNE Protocol"
abstract: >-
  LYNE is communication infrastructure for matters between parties without persistent personal addresses: a signed,
  versioned Thing and State, a purpose-bound and time-limited Grant, a temporary Live Line, and a Result signed by
  both parties that anchors the next State. LP 0.1 is the immutable baseline; LP 0.2 candidate-4 is an experimental
  candidate. The repository contains the specification texts, JSON Schemas, test vectors, examples and a
  language-neutral conformance kit.
